Silverstrand is currently looking for a suitably qualified Site Engineer for an immediate start on a large rail project located in South Brisbane.
We are looking for a person with a background in civil construction, including Earthworks, Drainage and Concrete Form/Reo/Pour. This role will be site based.
The successful candidate must have the following qualifications/ experience:
- Degree in Engineering or Construction Management or similar;
- Minimum of 2 years' onsite experience;
- Prior experience in an infrastructure or construction role;
- Thorough knowledge of codes and standards;
- A strong focus on WHS;
- Experience with SWMS, ITP's and quality documentation;
- Ability to read and understand drawings and specifications;
- A good understanding of MS Excel, Word Project etc;
Daily Tasks include:
- Ensuring compliance with safety & site environmental requirements;
- Provision of technical advice to stakeholders and clients;
- Management of sub-contractors and suppliers;
- Problem solving in relation to civil and structural requirements;
- Setting out and surveying;
- Procurement and management;
- Coordinating resources on site;
- Procurement of plant and materials;
- Inputting daily data onto MS spreadsheets;
- Record keeping;
- Programming of works; 
Must be willing to travel.
 Salary range between $100,000 - $110,000
If you believe you have the necessary experience and qualifications for this position, please forward a cover letter and your CV to employment@silverstrand.com.au.

About the business
EARTH AI is a fast-growing tech startup transforming the way critical metals are discovered. Founded in 2016 in Sydney, we are on a mission to secure the future of technology and infrastructure by responsibly sourcing the metals essential for global advancement. Using cutting-edge technology, we identify and develop new metal deposits with unmatched efficiency and sustainability. Our vision is to lead the industry by discovering and owning the majority of future metal deposits while becoming the most advanced, efficient, and responsible metal commodity company in the world.
About the role
Earth AI is looking for a graduate level geologist to analyse prospective areas in NSW and become an integral part of the operations team. You will be joining a team of passionate and motivated geologists, engineers and software developers, with the opportunity to grow your geological leadership skills as Earth AI continues to grow. 
What’s in it for you?
- Competitive compensation package, plus performance bonus;
- Team lunches;
- Company retreats;
- Professional development, and more.
Responsibilities include?
- Conducting geophysical surveys, soil and rock sampling, sample analysis using special equipment and geological mapping and other relevant data collection.
- Maintaining  the industry-best processes & practices for exploration activities. 
- Set and comply with QAQC standards for geological data collection, analysis, and interpretation.
- Promotion of safety mindset and professional excellence with colleagues and outsiders
- Cooperation with other staff or contractors performing geology-related
What’s essential?
- BSc Majoring in Geology;
- Field/outdoor experience;
- Excellent knowledge of geological features, as well as the ability to understand the geology of an area;
- Sydney based or willing to relocate to NSW;
- Available to commence work immediately;
